    "text": "Let <math><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be a twice differentiable function such that <math><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#39;</mi><mi>&#39;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> for all <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> If <math><mi>&#981;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> then <math><mi>&#981;</mi></math> is"
