  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0,2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#39;</mi><mi>&#39;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>&#160;</mi></math> for <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>0,2</mn><mo>]</mo></math><br />&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#39;</mi></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is increasing for <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>0,2</mn><mo>]</mo></math><br />Now, <math><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br />&nbsp; &nbsp; <math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#39;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#39;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mi>&#39;</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br />For <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>0,1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> , <math><mi>x</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mi>&#39;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>f</mi><mi>&#39;</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#981;</mi><mi>&#39;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />For <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>]</mo></math> , <math><mi>x</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#39;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#39;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#39;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Hence, <math><mi>&#981;</mi></math> is decreasing on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and increasing on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p>"
